<p><strong>Bottom line:</strong> I wasted $35 on unnecessary nutrients and 3 months of failed harvests. You don't have to. Check pH first, then nutrients, then water temp, then light distance, then roots. in that order. That 5-minute checklist would have saved me 12 weeks of frustration. If you need a pH test kit, <a href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=pH+test+kit+hydroponics+drops&tag=tabletopharve-20" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored">this $8 liquid test kit</a> is what I use. Never needs calibration, lasts me 6 months. For nutrients, the <a href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=General+Hydroponics+FloraSeries+nutrient+kit&tag=tabletopharve-20" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored">$35 FloraSeries starter</a> is all you need for lettuce. and you'll use it at quarter strength.</p>

